      "problem": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<1, \\\\ {e}^{(x-y)},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,0<y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =((0,1)\\cup (1,2))\\times (0,1) \\\\  & =((0,1)\\times (0,1))\\cup ((1,2)\\times (0,1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
